   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "y is a quotient whose numerator is the composite cos(2x), so the quotient rule opens the work: dy/dx = [x (cos(2x))' - cos(2x) * 1] / x^2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Power",
            "x",
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the chain rule, (cos(2x))' = -sin(2x) * 2 = -2 sin(2x).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            -2,
            [
               "Sin",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  "x"
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute into the quotient rule: dy/dx = [x(-2 sin(2x)) - cos(2x)] / x^2 = (-2x sin(2x) - cos(2x)) / x^2.",
